  "description": "RAGXEF crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H64 N12 O16 S6 Yb4,6(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Yb1 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Yb2 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors; Yb3 (Yb) has 7 O neighbors; Yb4 (Yb) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.501-3.785 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.11-111.09°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C96H64N12O16S6Yb4·6(C4H8O).",
